From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: report TX status when link wcid
 lookup fails

mt7996_mac_add_txs() drops the whole TXS event when
mt7996_rx_get_wcid() returns NULL (station teardown in progress,
wcid->sta not yet set, or an unexpected band index). If a status
tracked frame such as an association response is pending for that
wcid, its status skb is never completed; it times out HZ/4 later in
mt76_tx_status_skb_get() and gets reported to mac80211 without
IEEE80211_TX_STAT_ACK. hostapd then treats the frame as not
acknowledged and removes the station from the driver even though the
client acknowledged it.

Fall back to the primary wcid so the pending status skb is still
completed with the real TXS. The link wcid is only used for per-link
statistics and the poll list; the existing !link_wcid->sta check
keeps the fallback off the poll list.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1516,9 +1516,13 @@ static void mt7996_mac_add_txs(struct mt
 	if (!wcid)
 		goto out;
 
+	/* Fall back to the primary wcid so that a pending status skb is
+	 * still completed when the per-link lookup fails (e.g. station
+	 * teardown in progress); dropping the TXS here would leave the
+	 * skb to time out and get reported as not acknowledged. */
 	link_wcid = mt7996_rx_get_wcid(dev, wcidx, band);
 	if (!link_wcid)
-		goto out;
+		link_wcid = wcid;
 
 	mt7996_mac_add_txs_skb(dev, wcid, link_wcid, pid, txs_data);
 
